# sh-glyphs v1
# Accented letters built from a base letter and a mark of symbols.glyphs, plus the fallback glyph.
# `compose U+XXXX U+BASE mark`: the mark is centred over the letter's ink; over a lowercase letter it is merged into
# a new cell, over a capital it becomes a second part drawn above the cell.

# Fallback: drawn for any character no layer of the font has (a box with a question mark).
glyph U+FFFD advance 12
#########...
#.......#...
#..###..#...
#.#...#.#...
#.....#.#...
#....#..#...
#...#...#...
#...#...#...
#.......#...
#...#...#...
#.......#...
#########...
............
............
............
............

# Latin-1 capitals
compose U+00C0 U+0041 grave
compose U+00C1 U+0041 acute
compose U+00C2 U+0041 circumflex
compose U+00C3 U+0041 tilde
compose U+00C4 U+0041 diaeresis
compose U+00C5 U+0041 ring
compose U+00C8 U+0045 grave
compose U+00C9 U+0045 acute
compose U+00CA U+0045 circumflex
compose U+00CB U+0045 diaeresis
compose U+00CC U+0049 grave
compose U+00CD U+0049 acute
compose U+00CE U+0049 circumflex
compose U+00CF U+0049 diaeresis
compose U+00D1 U+004E tilde
compose U+00D2 U+004F grave
compose U+00D3 U+004F acute
compose U+00D4 U+004F circumflex
compose U+00D5 U+004F tilde
compose U+00D6 U+004F diaeresis
compose U+00D9 U+0055 grave
compose U+00DA U+0055 acute
compose U+00DB U+0055 circumflex
compose U+00DC U+0055 diaeresis
compose U+00DD U+0059 acute
compose U+0178 U+0059 diaeresis

# Latin-1 lowercase (the accented i stands on the dotless i of symbols.glyphs)
compose U+00E0 U+0061 grave
compose U+00E1 U+0061 acute
compose U+00E2 U+0061 circumflex
compose U+00E3 U+0061 tilde
compose U+00E4 U+0061 diaeresis
compose U+00E8 U+0065 grave
compose U+00E9 U+0065 acute
compose U+00EA U+0065 circumflex
compose U+00EB U+0065 diaeresis
compose U+00EC U+0131 grave
compose U+00ED U+0131 acute
compose U+00EE U+0131 circumflex
compose U+00EF U+0131 diaeresis
compose U+00F1 U+006E tilde
compose U+00F2 U+006F grave
compose U+00F3 U+006F acute
compose U+00F4 U+006F circumflex
compose U+00F5 U+006F tilde
compose U+00F6 U+006F diaeresis
compose U+00F9 U+0075 grave
compose U+00FA U+0075 acute
compose U+00FB U+0075 circumflex
compose U+00FC U+0075 diaeresis
compose U+00FD U+0079 acute
compose U+00FF U+0079 diaeresis
compose U+00E7 U+0063 cedilla below
compose U+00C7 U+0043 cedilla below

# Polish (ą ę ł Ą Ę Ł are whole letters in symbols.glyphs; ó is composed above)
compose U+0107 U+0063 acute
compose U+0144 U+006E acute
compose U+015B U+0073 acute
compose U+017A U+007A acute
compose U+017C U+007A dot
compose U+0106 U+0043 acute
compose U+0143 U+004E acute
compose U+015A U+0053 acute
compose U+0179 U+005A acute
compose U+017B U+005A dot

# Czech and Slovak
compose U+010D U+0063 caron
compose U+0161 U+0073 caron
compose U+017E U+007A caron
compose U+011B U+0065 caron
compose U+0159 U+0072 caron
compose U+0148 U+006E caron
compose U+016F U+0075 ring
compose U+010C U+0043 caron
compose U+0160 U+0053 caron
compose U+017D U+005A caron
compose U+011A U+0045 caron
compose U+0158 U+0052 caron
compose U+0147 U+004E caron
compose U+016E U+0055 ring

# Turkish: g with breve, s with cedilla, dotted capital I (the dotless i is in symbols.glyphs)
compose U+011F U+0067 breve
compose U+011E U+0047 breve
compose U+015F U+0073 cedilla below
compose U+015E U+0053 cedilla below
compose U+0130 U+0049 dot

# Cyrillic Ё ё and the Ukrainian/Belarusian letters that are Latin pictures
compose U+0401 U+0415 diaeresis
compose U+0451 U+0065 diaeresis
alias U+0406 U+0049
alias U+0456 U+0069
compose U+0407 U+0049 diaeresis
compose U+0457 U+0131 diaeresis
alias U+0408 U+004A
alias U+0458 U+006A

# cp1252 punctuation some translations carry as C1 control characters
alias U+0085 U+2026
alias U+0091 U+2018
alias U+0092 U+2019
alias U+0093 U+201C
alias U+0094 U+201D
alias U+0096 U+2013
alias U+0097 U+2014
alias U+008C U+0152
alias U+009C U+0153
